<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Ms. Spencer returns at the end of CBT-E; she had her twentieth session last week and has a written relapse-prevention plan with her own early warning signs (skipping meals, a run of long days, and feeling low) and what to do about each. She has had no binge eating or vomiting for six weeks. She eats three meals and two snacks every day and no longer weighs herself daily. Her end-of-treatment EDE-Q global score is 1.6. She takes fluoxetine 60 mg each morning without side effects. Her mood is good, she sleeps well, and she has had no thoughts of suicide or self-harm. She has told two close friends about her treatment. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Binge eating and vomiting</td><td>None for six weeks</td></tr><tr><td>CBT-E</td><td>Completed 20 sessions; written relapse-prevention plan</td></tr><tr><td>EDE-Q global score</td><td>1.6</td></tr><tr><td>Mood</td><td>Good; PHQ-9 4; item 9 scored 0</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

