    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Bulimia nervosa, severe, now in early remission (F50.23)</content>. No binge eating or vomiting for six weeks after 20 sessions of CBT-E with fluoxetine 60 mg; EDE-Q global score 1.6, from 3.9. Potassium 4.2 mmol/L. The coded problem stays active until remission is sustained. Relapse is most likely in the first year, so the relapse-prevention plan and fluoxetine continue. [S]<list><item>Continue fluoxetine 60 mg each morning for at least a year, then review a slow taper with Dr. Rosenthal.</item><item>Booster sessions with the therapist at one and three months.</item><item>Electrolytes only if vomiting returns.</item><item>Dental review as booked.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Major depressive disorder, recurrent, moderate, in remission (F33.1)</content>. PHQ-9 4, from 14: remission. Safety reviewed: no thoughts of suicide or self-harm; the safety plan and the 988 Suicide &amp; Crisis Lifeline remain in her phone. [S]<list><item>Continue fluoxetine; PHQ-9 at each visit.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Protocol monitoring: items the monitoring protocol calls for at this visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Measure</th><th>Interval</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Binge-eating and vomiting frequency (her self-monitoring record)</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>None for six weeks</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Eating Disorder Examination Questionnaire (EDE-Q) global score</td><td>Baseline, mid-treatment, and end of treatment</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Global score 1.6 at the end of treatment, from 3.9 at intake</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Weight and BMI</td><td>Every visit, and weekly in CBT-E sessions</td><td>Completed today</td><td>62.1 kg, BMI 19.6, steady through treatment</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Lying and standing pulse and blood pressure</td><td>Every visit while purging continues</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Lying 108/68, pulse 66; standing 108/70, pulse 72 (rise 6)</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Potassium, chloride, bicarbonate, and creatinine</td><td>Weekly until potassium is normal twice, then at each medical visit while purging continues</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Potassium 4.2 mmol/L; sodium 140, chloride 103, bicarbonate 25 mmol/L; creatinine 0.80 mg/dL, eGFR 102. Repeat only if vomiting returns</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Parotid and dental examination; dental protection</td><td>Every visit; a dental examination soon after diagnosis and regular dental reviews while vomiting continues</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Erosion stable; dental review in about three months</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Fluoxetine dose, adherence, and side effects (nausea, sleep, agitation, sexual effects, suicidal thoughts)</td><td>At the start, one to two weeks after starting or a dose change, then every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>60 mg; no side effects; continue for at least a year after remission</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>CBT-E attendance and progress</td><td>Up to 20 sessions over 20 weeks, twice weekly for the first four weeks</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Completed 20 sessions; relapse-prevention plan written; booster sessions at one and three months</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Regular eating and dietitian review</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Three meals and two snacks every day</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Depression measure (PHQ-9)</td><td>Monthly during acute treatment, then periodically</td><td>Completed today</td><td>PHQ-9 4, item 9 scored 0: remission</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Suicide-risk review, safety plan, lethal means, and the 988 Suicide &amp; Crisis Lifeline</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No thoughts of suicide or self-harm; safety plan and the 988 Suicide &amp; Crisis Lifeline current</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Goal progress:</paragraph><list><item>No binge eating or vomiting for at least four weeks by the end of 20 weeks of CBT-E. Outcome by 2026-07-13: No binge eating or vomiting for six weeks [S]</item><item>Potassium at least 3.5 mmol/L on two checks within four weeks. Outcome by 2026-03-16: Potassium 3.6 and 3.9 mmol/L; supplement stopped [S]</item><item>Regular eating (three meals and two or three snacks) on most days by three months. Outcome by 2026-05-11: Regular eating on six or seven days a week [S]</item><item>PHQ-9 score below 5 by the end of treatment. Outcome by 2026-07-13: PHQ-9 4 [S]</item><item>EDE-Q global score below 2.0 by the end of treatment. Outcome by 2026-07-13: EDE-Q global score 1.6 [S]</item></list><paragraph>Guideline basis: The American Psychiatric Association Practice Guideline for the Treatment of Patients With Eating Disorders, Fourth Edition (2023); Eating disorders: recognition and treatment (NICE guideline NG69) (2017, updated 2020); Depression and Suicide Risk in Adults: Screening (2023); VA/DoD Clinical Practice Guideline for Assessment and Management of Patients at Risk for Suicide (2024); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, depression, bipolar, and mood disorders monograph (2026)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Booster CBT-E sessions at one and three months. Visit in three months, sooner for any return of bingeing or vomiting. Psychiatry review of fluoxetine after a year of remission. [S]</paragraph></text>

